1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:09,374
Every day, a bank gets thousands of alerts
saying a card payment might be fraud.

2
00:00:09,633 --> 00:00:10,730
A thief?

3
00:00:10,967 --> 00:00:13,945
Or a customer on holiday with a new phone?

4
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:17,648
Block the wrong card, you lose a customer.

5
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:21,244
Miss the thief, the bank loses money.

6
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:25,314
This AI makes that call,
and shows its work.

7
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:27,706
Twenty alerts.

8
00:00:27,967 --> 00:00:32,746
For each, the agent decides
the kind of fraud, or that the

9
00:00:32,786 --> 00:00:38,520
customer is innocent, and the next
best action, with who approves it.

10
00:00:38,767 --> 00:00:41,666
Here is the trap.

11
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:45,348
The bank score is close to a decoy.

12
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:45,835
All nine hundred cleared
cases scored high.

13
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:48,869
A third of confirmed fraud scored low.

14
00:00:49,967 --> 00:00:52,265
Fraud lives in the connections.

15
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:55,060
One rare phone setup, across many cards.

16
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:57,285
Purchases kept just under a limit.

17
00:00:57,533 --> 00:01:00,459
So everything goes into
a graph, in TigerGraph.

18
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:02,868
Five hundred and ninety thousand payments.

19
00:01:03,133 --> 00:01:04,701
Fourteen thousand cards.

20
00:01:04,967 --> 00:01:07,448
A graph finds those links in milliseconds.

21
00:01:08,533 --> 00:01:09,970
Four parts.

22
00:01:10,233 --> 00:01:12,036
A console in your browser.

23
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:14,912
The agent, a TypeScript program.

24
00:01:15,167 --> 00:01:18,303
TigerGraph in the cloud,
reached only through

25
00:01:18,343 --> 00:01:21,802
sixteen installed GSQL
queries on the MCP server.

26
00:01:22,067 --> 00:01:24,130
And Ollama for the words.

27
00:01:24,367 --> 00:01:25,960
The graph analyses.

28
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:27,767
The rules decide.

29
00:01:28,033 --> 00:01:29,653
The AI explains.

30
00:01:30,733 --> 00:01:37,055
Every case is frozen at the moment
it opened, so there is no look-ahead.

31
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:43,184
Then two advocates run at once:
a prosecutor hunting fraud, and a

32
00:01:43,224 --> 00:01:49,787
defence hunting the innocent explanation,
like a holiday or a new phone.

33
00:01:50,033 --> 00:01:54,970
A judge weighs them, and the rules choose.

34
00:01:56,067 --> 00:01:57,712
The guardrails.

35
00:01:57,967 --> 00:02:01,833
The easy way to win a
demo is to make things up.

36
00:02:02,067 --> 00:02:07,213
The customer reply is not in the
data, so we do not invent one.

37
00:02:07,467 --> 00:02:11,045
Every identifier is
checked against the graph.

38
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:15,009
If the model fails, the
case stops with an error.

39
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:18,190
The honest scorecard.

40
00:02:18,433 --> 00:02:22,508
Three hundred past cases
replayed with no look-ahead.

41
00:02:22,767 --> 00:02:26,372
Area under the curve, point seven seven.

42
00:02:26,633 --> 00:02:30,813
Likely fraud is right
ninety-seven percent of the time.

43
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:35,481
But calibration drifts, and naming
the pattern still needs work.

44
00:02:36,567 --> 00:02:38,474
So, let us actually run it.

45
00:02:38,733 --> 00:02:40,588
Terminal first, then the browser.

46
00:02:41,667 --> 00:02:43,051
A health check.

47
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:45,603
Reachable, the secret
works, and TigerGraph

48
00:02:45,643 --> 00:02:48,368
comes back with version
four point two point five.

49
00:02:49,867 --> 00:02:50,859
Then the tests.

50
00:02:51,100 --> 00:02:54,197
A hundred and thirty-eight,
in about two seconds,

51
00:02:54,237 --> 00:02:57,631
and the same suite runs
against the live cloud graph.

52
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:01,242
Now, one real alert.

53
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:04,687
Number fourteen.

54
00:03:04,933 --> 00:03:09,113
The bank score is point zero five.

55
00:03:09,367 --> 00:03:15,897
By that score, this customer is innocent.

56
00:03:16,133 --> 00:03:19,190
Watch what the graph finds.

57
00:03:20,667 --> 00:03:22,495
Likely fraud.

58
00:03:22,733 --> 00:03:28,010
Ninety-four percent.

59
00:03:28,267 --> 00:03:29,521
Forty-four customers share
one rare device profile.

60
00:03:29,767 --> 00:03:34,103
Always new.

61
00:03:34,367 --> 00:03:35,176
Always behind an anonymous proxy.

62
00:03:35,433 --> 00:03:37,184
The score never saw it.

63
00:03:37,433 --> 00:03:39,735
So: monitor the linked cards, open a case,

64
00:03:39,775 --> 00:03:42,841
escalate, and file a report
that needs a fraud manager.

65
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:45,791
The rules chose that, not the AI.

66
00:03:47,267 --> 00:03:50,480
And now I break the model on purpose.

67
00:03:50,733 --> 00:03:52,222
The case stops.

68
00:03:52,467 --> 00:03:55,836
A clear error, and no file is written.

69
00:03:56,100 --> 00:03:59,287
No invented text, no quiet fallback.

70
00:04:00,767 --> 00:04:02,935
And the backtest.

71
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:10,096
Three hundred past cases, replayed as if
new, each frozen at its own opening moment.

72
00:04:10,333 --> 00:04:12,919
These numbers are being produced live.

73
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:16,229
Now the console.

74
00:04:16,467 --> 00:04:19,866
Pick the alert, press
Investigate, and every step

75
00:04:19,906 --> 00:04:23,415
appears as it happens,
with what it found and why.

76
00:04:23,667 --> 00:04:27,010
The signs of fraud, and
the signs of innocence.

77
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:30,610
The next best action,
with its approval buttons.

78
00:04:30,867 --> 00:04:33,792
Every line comes from a real log.

79
00:04:35,767 --> 00:04:38,510
So that is it.

80
00:04:38,767 --> 00:04:42,633
A graph that finds the links.

81
00:04:42,867 --> 00:04:46,106
Rules that decide.

82
00:04:46,367 --> 00:04:50,416
An AI that only explains.

83
00:04:50,667 --> 00:04:53,383
And nothing made up.

84
00:04:53,633 --> 00:04:54,809
Thank you.
